<section class="surface mt-6 rounded-2xl p-6"><h2 class="font-semibold">Sign every API request</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">Send X-UPI-Timestamp (Unix seconds), X-UPI-Nonce (unique, 16–128 characters), and X-UPI-Signature (hex HMAC-SHA256). Sign METHOD, path including query string, timestamp, nonce and SHA256(raw body), separated by newline characters. Use the secret portion after the third underscore of your API token as the HMAC key. Requests expire after five minutes. Rotate legacy keys issued before request signing was added.</p></section>
<section class="surface mt-6 rounded-2xl p-6"><h2 class="font-semibold">Integration flow</h2><ol class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-muted"><li>Your server creates an order and saves its gateway ID, exact payable amount and currency before opening checkout.</li><li>Verify the raw webhook signature and fetch <code>/api/v1/orders/{id}?event_id={event_id}</code> with a separate read key.</li><li>Require paid status, matching order, amount, currency, reference hash, event sequence and verification hash. Manual confirmations require your explicit acceptance.</li><li>Atomically record the event and enqueue fulfillment once. Return HTTP 200 and acknowledge the event after the database commit.</li><li>Run the daily merchant integrity check and alert on verification mismatches. Browser redirects and popup callbacks never authorize fulfillment.</li></ol><p class="mt-4 text-xs text-muted">The repository includes a Laravel package, a WooCommerce plugin, PHP/Node/Python examples and <code>/hx-checkout.js</code> for popup checkout.</p></section>
